{%- comment -%}
  TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC — not an email. Paste into the Custom Liquid block of the
  browse-abandonment automation, open the PREVIEW, read what it prints, then
  delete it and paste the real template back.

  Why this exists: Shopify Email's browse-abandonment Liquid scope is not
  documented and differs between stores. Rather than guess which object holds
  the viewed products, this prints every plausible candidate so you can see
  which one is actually populated.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;background:#fff;padding:16px;color:#111;">
<b style="font-size:14px;">BROWSE ABANDONMENT — WHAT IS AVAILABLE</b><br><br>

<b>Singular product</b><br>
product.title ......... [{{ product.title }}]<br>
product.url ........... [{{ product.url }}]<br>
product.featured_image  [{{ product.featured_image }}]<br>
product.image ......... [{{ product.image }}]<br><br>

<b>Collections that might hold several</b><br>
products.size ......... [{{ products.size }}]<br>
line_items.size ....... [{{ line_items.size }}]<br>
product_recommendations.size [{{ product_recommendations.size }}]<br>
viewed_products.size .. [{{ viewed_products.size }}]<br>
recently_viewed.size .. [{{ recently_viewed.size }}]<br>
abandonment.products.size [{{ abandonment.products.size }}]<br><br>

<b>Customer + shop</b><br>
customer.first_name ... [{{ customer.first_name }}]<br>
customer.email ........ [{{ customer.email }}]<br>
shop.name ............. [{{ shop.name }}]<br>
shop.url .............. [{{ shop.url }}]<br><br>

<b>First item of whichever collection is populated</b><br>
{% for p in products %}products[{{ forloop.index0 }}] = [{{ p.title }}] img=[{{ p.image }}]<br>{% endfor %}
{% for p in product_recommendations %}rec[{{ forloop.index0 }}] = [{{ p.title }}]<br>{% endfor %}
{% for p in viewed_products %}viewed[{{ forloop.index0 }}] = [{{ p.title }}]<br>{% endfor %}
{% for p in line_items %}line[{{ forloop.index0 }}] = [{{ p.title }}]<br>{% endfor %}

<br><b>Anything in [ ] that is not empty is the object to use.</b>
</div>
